{"scenario":"sis-flow-state-per-client","rows":["S-0163","S-0019","S-0022","S-0023","S-0027","S-0028","S-0021","A-0109","S-0161","C-1050"],"source":"Ed4 S.4.1, p.S-5","description":"Flow control is per client: S_DATA_FLOW_OFF to one client does not hold off another bound client, whose U_PDUs are accepted while the first is off, and the first stays off and gets S_DATA_FLOW_ON on its own count alone.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":256,"block_ms":4800}]}},"note":"The external busy input holds the channel busy from 0 (P5-4), so nothing goes on air (K-0066). Conn 1 binds SAP 5 and conn 2 binds SAP 6, both for non-ARQ (Transmission Mode 2, no confirmation); each gets S_BIND_ACCEPTED with MTU 2048 and flow on with no S_DATA_FLOW_ON (interp S-0027). At 0 conn 1 sends the eight 2048-byte U_PDUs of sis/flow-off-discard-rejected (SAP 5 at 0.0.1.3, DELIVERY MODE default, TTL 30, so TTD 60000): the first starts dts.ttd (C-1050) and the eighth brings conn 1 to eight MTUs, so conn 1 alone is sent S_DATA_FLOW_OFF (S-0019, S-0022; interp S-0163). At 1000 conn 2 sends 'ok' (TTL 10, TTD 21000): conn 2 has nothing counted and its flow is on, so it is accepted and, being the new earliest TTD, restarts dts.ttd for 20000 ms (C-1050); conn 2 is sent nothing. Then conn 1 sends 'ping' with DELIVERY MODE ARQ and node confirmation: conn 1 is still off, so it is discarded and rejected with reason 13, Data Buffers Full (S-0023, A-0109; interp S-0028), with no soft link asked for. At 21000 dts.ttd expires: the DTS rejects conn 2's U_PDU for TTL and re-arms for 60000; conn 2 asked for no confirmation and was never off, so it is sent nothing, and conn 1, still at eight MTUs, gets no S_DATA_FLOW_ON. At 60000 the eight are rejected and after the fourth conn 1 is at four MTUs and gets S_DATA_FLOW_ON (S-0021; interp S-0163). Conn 2 is sent nothing throughout."}
